1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:02,120
Luke 20

2
00:00:02,120 --> 00:00:08,080
One day, as Jesus was teaching the people in the temple and preaching the gospel,

3
00:00:08,660 --> 00:00:12,480
the chief priests and the scribes with the elders came up and said to him,

4
00:00:13,200 --> 00:00:17,160
Tell us by what authority you do these things, or who it is that gave you this authority?

5
00:00:17,920 --> 00:00:18,820
He answered them,

6
00:00:19,560 --> 00:00:21,760
I also will ask you a question.

7
00:00:22,360 --> 00:00:27,600
Now tell me, was the baptism of John from heaven or from man?

8
00:00:27,600 --> 00:00:30,500
And they discussed it with one another, saying,

9
00:00:31,280 --> 00:00:35,020
If we say, From heaven, he will say, Why did you not believe him?

10
00:00:35,260 --> 00:00:38,780
But if we say, From man, all the people will stone us to death,

11
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:41,240
for they are convinced that John was a prophet.

12
00:00:41,780 --> 00:00:44,740
So they answered that they did not know where it came from.

13
00:00:45,440 --> 00:00:46,720
And Jesus said to them,

14
00:00:47,460 --> 00:00:51,700
Neither will I tell you by what authority I do these things.

15
00:00:52,140 --> 00:00:54,460
And he began to tell the people this parable.

16
00:00:54,800 --> 00:00:56,640
A man planted a vineyard,

17
00:00:56,640 --> 00:00:58,200
and led it out to tenants,

18
00:00:58,620 --> 00:01:01,260
and went into another country for a long while.

19
00:01:02,020 --> 00:01:05,140
When the time came, he sent a servant to the tenants,

20
00:01:05,520 --> 00:01:08,320
so that they would give him some of the fruit of the vineyard.

21
00:01:08,780 --> 00:01:12,000
But the tenants beat him and sent him away empty-handed.

22
00:01:12,600 --> 00:01:14,060
And he sent another servant,

23
00:01:14,600 --> 00:01:17,160
but they also beat and treated him shamefully,

24
00:01:17,400 --> 00:01:19,200
and sent him away empty-handed.

25
00:01:19,700 --> 00:01:21,880
And he sent yet a third.

26
00:01:22,520 --> 00:01:25,640
This one also they wounded and cast out.

27
00:01:26,640 --> 00:01:28,540
Then the owner of the vineyard said,

28
00:01:28,940 --> 00:01:30,020
What shall I do?

29
00:01:30,680 --> 00:01:32,960
I will send my beloved son.

30
00:01:33,480 --> 00:01:35,000
Perhaps they will respect him.

31
00:01:35,600 --> 00:01:38,100
But when the tenants saw him, they said to themselves,

32
00:01:38,620 --> 00:01:40,180
This is the heir.

33
00:01:40,560 --> 00:01:43,420
Let us kill him, so that the inheritance may be ours.

34
00:01:44,100 --> 00:01:47,040
And they threw him out of the vineyard and killed him.

35
00:01:48,060 --> 00:01:50,840
What then will the owner of the vineyard do to them?

36
00:01:51,220 --> 00:01:56,020
He will come and destroy those tenants and give the vineyard to others.

37
00:01:56,640 --> 00:01:58,340
When they heard this, they said,

38
00:01:58,980 --> 00:01:59,920
Surely not.

39
00:02:00,680 --> 00:02:02,700
But he looked directly at them and said,

40
00:02:03,400 --> 00:02:05,280
What then is this that is written?

41
00:02:05,780 --> 00:02:09,560
The stone that the builders rejected has become the cornerstone.

42
00:02:10,340 --> 00:02:13,520
Everyone who falls on that stone will be broken to pieces,

43
00:02:14,120 --> 00:02:17,880
and when it falls on anyone, it will crush him.

44
00:02:18,260 --> 00:02:22,980
The scribes and the chief priests sought to lay hands on him at that very hour,

45
00:02:23,400 --> 00:02:26,480
for they perceived that he had told this parable against them.

46
00:02:26,900 --> 00:02:28,240
But they feared the people.

47
00:02:29,100 --> 00:02:32,600
So they watched him and sent spies who pretended to be sincere,

48
00:02:32,900 --> 00:02:34,980
that they might catch him in something he said,

49
00:02:34,980 --> 00:02:39,180
so as to deliver him up to the authority and jurisdiction of the governor.

50
00:02:39,960 --> 00:02:40,820
So they asked him,

51
00:02:41,380 --> 00:02:48,680
Teacher, we know that you speak and teach rightly and show no partiality,

52
00:02:49,300 --> 00:02:51,980
but truly teach the way of God.

53
00:02:53,200 --> 00:02:56,520
Is it lawful for us to give tribute to Caesar?

54
00:02:56,640 --> 00:02:58,000
Or not?

55
00:02:58,680 --> 00:03:01,600
But he perceived their craftiness and said to them,

56
00:03:02,460 --> 00:03:03,600
Show me a denarius.

57
00:03:04,580 --> 00:03:07,120
Whose likeness and inscription does it have?

58
00:03:07,840 --> 00:03:08,600
They said,

59
00:03:09,320 --> 00:03:10,520
Caesar's.

60
00:03:11,080 --> 00:03:12,140
He said to them,

61
00:03:12,940 --> 00:03:15,740
Then render to Caesar the things that are Caesar's,

62
00:03:16,140 --> 00:03:18,620
and to God the things that are God's.

63
00:03:19,300 --> 00:03:23,200
And they were not able in the presence of the people to catch him in what he said,

64
00:03:23,200 --> 00:03:26,140
but marveling at his answer they became silent.

65
00:03:26,640 --> 00:03:29,900
There came to him some Sadducees,

66
00:03:30,020 --> 00:03:32,280
those who deny that there is a resurrection,

67
00:03:32,280 --> 00:03:34,480
and they asked him a question, saying,

68
00:03:34,920 --> 00:03:40,680
Teacher, Moses wrote for us that if a man's brother dies,

69
00:03:40,800 --> 00:03:42,660
having a wife but no children,

70
00:03:43,100 --> 00:03:47,240
the man must take the widow and raise up offspring for his brother.

71
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:50,260
Now there were seven brothers.

72
00:03:50,800 --> 00:03:54,200
The first took a wife and died without children,

73
00:03:54,940 --> 00:03:56,620
and the second and the third died without children.

74
00:03:56,620 --> 00:03:57,240
The third took her,

75
00:03:57,640 --> 00:04:01,600
and likewise all seven left no children and died.

76
00:04:02,740 --> 00:04:04,920
Afterward the woman also died.

77
00:04:05,820 --> 00:04:07,880
In the resurrection, therefore,

78
00:04:08,500 --> 00:04:10,700
whose wife will the woman be?

79
00:04:11,220 --> 00:04:13,420
For the seven had her as wife.

80
00:04:14,220 --> 00:04:15,480
And Jesus said to them,

81
00:04:16,180 --> 00:04:19,860
The sons of this age marry and are given in marriage.

82
00:04:20,460 --> 00:04:23,980
But those who are considered worthy to attain to that age

83
00:04:23,980 --> 00:04:26,120
and to the resurrection from the dead,

84
00:04:26,620 --> 00:04:28,680
neither marry nor are given in marriage.

85
00:04:29,160 --> 00:04:31,080
For they cannot die any more,

86
00:04:31,460 --> 00:04:33,380
because they are equal to angels

87
00:04:33,380 --> 00:04:35,240
and are sons of God,

88
00:04:35,680 --> 00:04:37,300
being sons of the resurrection.

89
00:04:38,400 --> 00:04:40,320
But that the dead are raised,

90
00:04:40,800 --> 00:04:41,980
even Moses showed,

91
00:04:42,460 --> 00:04:44,000
in the passage about the bush,

92
00:04:44,480 --> 00:04:47,140
where he calls the Lord the God of Abraham

93
00:04:47,140 --> 00:04:50,020
and the God of Isaac and the God of Jacob.

94
00:04:50,680 --> 00:04:52,600
Now he is not God of the dead,

95
00:04:52,600 --> 00:04:53,960
but of the living,

96
00:04:54,520 --> 00:04:56,200
for all live to him.

97
00:04:56,620 --> 00:04:58,760
Then some of the scribes answered,

98
00:04:59,440 --> 00:05:01,620
Teacher, you have spoken well.

99
00:05:02,340 --> 00:05:05,120
For they no longer dared to ask him any question.

100
00:05:05,740 --> 00:05:06,780
But he said to them,

101
00:05:07,400 --> 00:05:11,100
How can they say that the Christ is David's son?

102
00:05:11,660 --> 00:05:14,380
For David himself says in the book of Psalms,

103
00:05:15,060 --> 00:05:16,880
The Lord said to my Lord,

104
00:05:17,220 --> 00:05:18,520
Sit at my right hand,

105
00:05:18,820 --> 00:05:21,160
until I make your enemies your footstool.

106
00:05:21,900 --> 00:05:23,660
David thus calls him Lord.

107
00:05:23,920 --> 00:05:26,340
So how is he his son?

108
00:05:27,080 --> 00:05:29,060
And in the hearing of all the people,

109
00:05:29,160 --> 00:05:30,320
he said to his disciples,

110
00:05:31,200 --> 00:05:32,760
Beware of the scribes,

111
00:05:33,020 --> 00:05:35,540
who like to walk around in long robes,

112
00:05:35,760 --> 00:05:37,820
and love greetings in the marketplaces,

113
00:05:38,180 --> 00:05:40,240
and the best seats in the synagogues,

114
00:05:40,380 --> 00:05:42,380
and the places of honor at feasts,

115
00:05:42,680 --> 00:05:44,680
who devour widows' houses,

116
00:05:45,060 --> 00:05:47,580
and for a pretense make long prayers.

117
00:05:47,580 --> 00:05:50,580
They will receive the greater condemnation.

